{"anchor":"business at the office","spark":"unable to speak with duke","wound":"fear of unready fleet","fuel":"wanting peace","bridge":null,"echo":"god send us peace","narrative":"The writer spent the morning full of business at the office, dined with Mr. Povy, and went to my Lord Chancellor's, where he could not speak with the Duke of Albemarle because the King and Council were busy. He bought four bands from his new pretty seamstress and found his house mighty neat and clean. He records that French ambassadors have come incognito, and that the fleet has lain a good while at Harwich, and he is sure we are unable to set out another small fleet if this one is worsted, so he cries 'God send us peace!' On the Lord's day he went to church with his wife in her new light-coloured silk gown, and in the evening walked in the garden with Lady Pen and her daughter, eating together and being very merry before bed.","wound_note":null}

